  "body": "Closing without merging after mathematical and priority review.\n\nThe submitted counterexample is mathematically sound, but the complete negative answer already appears in §3.44, p.60, of [Results on problems from the Kourovka Notebook](https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kourovka-mathematics.pdf), credited to Codex gpt-6-astra, Michael Kinyon and Josef Urban (Version 4, dated 19 September 2026). We independently checked the ordinary-free-ultrafilter Boolean group, dense support-size partition and obstruction to every disjoint finite-block sequence; no mathematical gap was found.\n\nThe [Internet Archive capture of 2 October 2026](https://web.archive.org/web/20261002014549id_/https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kourovka-mathematics.pdf) is byte-for-byte identical to the current PDF, including that complete proof, and predates this PR's creation on 8 October. We do not assign ultimate first discovery or claim referee acceptance.\n\nAttribution repairs credit but cannot make this same resolved target a new solution. The optional checker error-format issue was repaired separately; that does not change the priority outcome. Original evidence and the declared 1/5 author record are preserved. This closure creates no merge, new preprint, DOI, tracker row or native-ledger change.\n\n<!-- PR967-PRIORITY-CLOSURE-v1:b356dec5cb01e5f536b9cfeece56ad08844c03cb -->\n",
